KG42.register("slice-clusters-a3190d50e76e2da4e23c9bf4",{"id":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v142-d-K003","paper":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading","title":"Parameter setting, information acquisition, and settlement of non-collaborative hierarchical billing","source_pointer":"/clusters/151","node_ids":["COMP-1494fb13645c04a4","COMP-ebd853401562a305","COMP-d839969e92ed0c6e"],"rule_refs":["38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R007","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R008","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R010"],"visible_rule_refs":["38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R007","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R008","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R010"],"suppressed_rule_refs":[],"edges":[{"global_edge_id":"S-4599e39fcbe63e9c","source":"COMP-1494fb13645c04a4","target":"COMP-d839969e92ed0c6e","type":"links","assertion_ids":["38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R010::E::v141-c-R010-E001"],"rule_refs":["38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R010"],"internal":false}],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"interface_annotations":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g01-E18"],"rationale":"The source places the information update of the aggregator and ECS and the customer acquisition of information in the same iterative process; the two Rule-Chains respectively provide the supply activity and the acquisition requirement."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::theta-alpha","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::theta_alpha","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"The penalty factor set in advance and the average energy consumption definition correspond respectively to the rate multiplier and the segment threshold of the hierarchical bill, and no new parameter-tuning decision or dynamic update formula is added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E18"],"rationale":"The acquired total energy consumption and mean correspond to the input contents of the billing base rate and threshold; this is a functional correspondence between information and the billing function, and it does not imply that every iteration produces a settled bill."}],"annotation_policy":"Original D connections are annotations, not additional S edges.","empty_after_chain_suppression":false});
